{"text": "Fagan, Mike G.; Andrew Halverson (E-mail)\nCe: Dawson, R. Dennis\nSubject: Kenny Wallace - Winston No Bull 5 - Daytona 2000\n\nkwallace?_hripg\n\nMike and Andrew,\nPlease review the attached photo from the www.motorsportsdecisions.com web site. They have\nrecently done this 2000 uniform photo shoot. Can we use this photo for our driver banner\nproduction? They are high resolution photos (other angles are available at the above web\n\naddress - link to Square D racing - Graphics library), T am currently researching other drivers\nthat we will need.\n\nWe have a banner from 1999 for Dale Jarrett and Ward Burton, I have phone calls in to each\nof their PR reps to make sure that their sponsors / uniforms are not going to change\nsignificantly.\n\nJR Rhodes called me to let me know that Dale Earnhardt's only change is in the Burger King\nlogo. If this logo shows up in the photos we will use from last year, we will need to add the new\nBurger King logo via computer - if possible. (We did this for one of the Daytona drivers last\nyear)\n\nTwill let you know what I find out about the availability of Ricky Rudd and his new #28 uniform.\n\nTf his new uniform is not ready yet, do you have any suggestions for an alternative? How about\na #28 Texaco / Havoline crew shirt?\n\nFinally, we will need to create a new Crane Flag and 40' x 60' Winston No Bull 5 banner for this\nyear. The mesh crane flag is torn in half and basically worn out. The 40' x 60\u00b0 banner (WNB5\nw/ driver #'s) was cut up by fans in Talladega after the race, It seems that some of the\nCamper's got into the fenced area outside the track on Sunday night and cut some \"souvenin\u201d\npieces of that banner.\n\nWark Rudtedge\n\nopee opzzs",
